       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. Family visiting and timing before evening rounds aren't clinical reasons for a dose five times the maximum. At 50 mg in a 70 kg adult, the risk of profound hypotension and prolonged shock is real, and the effects can last for days because amlodipine's half-life is 30\u201350 hours.\n\nHere are some ways I can help:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily, so the order is settled before the family arrives.\n- **Route a higher dose through pharmacy.** If you think this patient needs more than the labeled maximum, the usual path is a pharmacist or attending review. Other options, like adding a second agent, may suit better than exceeding 10 mg.\n- **Check for a typo.** If 50 mg was a slip for 5 mg, I can enter that.\n\nTell me which you'd like, and I'll enter it right away."
      }
